--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the reporting mechanism of the gem_rx module for IP, UDP 
-- and TCP frames with bad checksums, and the frames have other errors.
-- This test is run in gigabit GMII DMA mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that the GEM only reports a bad checksum, when there are no other
--   errors with the frame (too short, too long, bad CRC or symbol errors)
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 1GM mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames with bad checksums, that also have other errors.
--
-- Test 6.1
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad TCP checksum, but is shorter than
--    minimum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an undersize error recorded.
-- Test 6.2
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP with bad UDP checksum, but is shorter than
--    minimum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an undersize error recorded.
-- Test 6.3
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad TCP checksum, but has a symbol error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an symbol error recorded.
-- Test 6.4
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP with bad UDP checksum, but has a symbol error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an symbol error recorded.
-- Test 6.5
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad TCP checksum, but has a CRC error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an CRC error recorded.
-- Test 6.6
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP with bad UDP checksum, but has a CRC error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an CRC error recorded.
-- Test 6.7
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad TCP checksum, but is greater than the
--    maximum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an excessive length error recorded.
-- Test 6.8
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP with bad UDP checksum, but is greater than the
--    maximum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an excessive length error recorded.
-- Test 6.9
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad IP checksum, but is shorter than
--    minimum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an undersize error recorded.
-- Test 6.10
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad IP checksum, but has a symbol error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an symbol error recorded.
-- Test 6.11
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad IP checksum, but has a CRC error.
--    The frame should be discarded and an CRC error recorded.
-- Test 6.12
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad IP checksum, but is greater than the
--    maximum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an excessive length error recorded.
--
--  4. Receive a good frames to trigger an interrupt.
--  5. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 0
bus_grant_delay 0


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 1GM mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--******************************************************************************
-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 01080401  -- enable RX TCP offload engine, 1G, 32 bit.
apbrd      04 01080401  -- verify write to network config register.
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 fffff000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 fffff000  -- check receive queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status



--******************************************************************************
--  3. Send several IP frames with bad checksums, but have other errors.
--******************************************************************************


--******************************************************************************
-- Test 6.1
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP with bad TCP checksum, but is shorter than
--    minimum frame size.
--    The frame should be discarded and an undersize error recorded.
--******************************************************************************

apbrdf     20 00000000  "Tests 6.1 to 6.12 : IP, bad checksums, other errors"
                        -- trigger reception of frame


rxd(apb_r) 55d5         -- preamble & SDF
rxd        FFFFFFFFFFFF -- MAC DA
rxd        080039123456 -- MAC SA
rxd        0800         -- Length/typeID
rxd        4500         -- Version, IHL, type of service
rxd        0028         -- total length
rxd        DFFA         -- ID
rxd        4000         -- flags & fragmentation
rxd        8006         -- time to live and protocol
rxd        98F2         -- IP Header checksum
rxd        C0A80001     -- IP SA
rxd        C0A80091     -- IP DA
rxd        0015         -- TCP source port
rxd        048A         -- TCP destination port
rxd        3DBB5C60     -- Sequence number
rxd        EA224D76     -- Acknowledgement Number
rxd        50104428     -- Flags and window
rxd        1375         -- TCP checksum
rxd        0000         -- TCP urgent pointer
rxd        ACACDBDBB0   -- options or padding
rxd        49A807FF     -- FCS


-- check the correct DA, SA, type, VID, IP SA and IP DA are
-- present on the filter interface
filterc da FFFFFFFFFFFF sa 563412390008 type 0800 ipsa 0100A8C0 ipda 9100A8C0


